---
title: "US 1.0.1, 1.0.3, 1.0.4: Add User Profiles / Show history of Site Inspections on a Steward's Profile / Aggregate User Activity and Contributions on a user's profile"
config:
  theme: base
  sequence:
    actorMargin: 70
    boxMargin: 12
    diagramMarginX: 45
    diagramMarginY: 30
    messageMargin: 38
    noteMargin: 16
    mirrorActors: true
    width: 200
    height: 90
  themeVariables:
    background: "#ffffff"
    primaryColor: "#69a8ef"
    primaryBorderColor: "#333333"
    primaryTextColor: "#111111"
    actorBkg: "#69a8ef"
    actorBorder: "#333333"
    actorTextColor: "#111111"
    actorLineColor: "#555555"
    signalColor: "#333333"
    signalTextColor: "#111111"
    activationBkgColor: "#cdd3db"
    activationBorderColor: "#cdd3db"
    noteBkgColor: "#ffe344"
    noteBorderColor: "#d4ba24"
    noteTextColor: "#111111"
    labelBoxBkgColor: "#ffffff"
    labelBoxBorderColor: "#555555"
    labelTextColor: "#111111"
    loopTextColor: "#111111"
    altBackground: "#ffffff"
  themeCSS: |
    .actor-line {
      stroke-dasharray: 10 10 !important;
      stroke-width: 1.25px !important;
    }
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Steward
    participant Pages as Web pages<br/>HeaderDropdown menu,<br/>/detail/[namesite]
    participant Profile as Profile page<br/>/profile, /people/[personId]<br/>components/ProfilePage.tsx
    participant Actions as API route<br/>GET /api/profile<br/>app/api/profile/route.ts
    participant StewardActions as Server actions<br/>utils/steward-actions.ts,<br/>utils/supabase/queries.ts
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>PostgreSQL

    Note over Steward,DB: Covers US 1.0.1, 1.0.3 and 1.0.4. "(Proposed)" = the step is not in the code on main as of October 7, 2026.

    alt Open own profile (1.0.1 AT2)
        Steward->>Pages: Select "My profile" in HeaderDropdown (router.push('/profile'))
        Pages->>Profile: Open /profile of signed-in user
    else Open profile from "Submitted by" on a Site page (1.0.1 AT3)
        Pages->>StewardActions: getPersonByAuthUserId(user_id) in utils/steward-actions.ts<br/>(SubmittedBy.tsx, when the SIR loads)
        StewardActions-->>Pages: people id and display_name
        Steward->>Pages: Select "Submitted by" name on a SIR on /detail/[namesite]
        Pages->>Profile: Open /people/{people.id}
    else Open profile from "Steward:" on a Site page (1.0.1 AT3)
        Pages->>StewardActions: getSiteSteward(siteId) in utils/steward-actions.ts<br/>(SiteSteward.tsx, when the page loads)
        StewardActions-->>Pages: people id and display_name
        Steward->>Pages: Select the "Steward:" link on /detail/[namesite]
        Pages->>Profile: Open /people/{people.id}
    end
    activate Profile

    Profile->>Actions: fetch GET /api/profile?personId={people.id}<br/>(own profile: no personId, page defaults to 1)
    activate Actions
    Actions->>Actions: requireUser(): auth.getUser() from session cookie
    Note right of Actions: Session checked on server. Approval is checked only<br/>in the client ProtectedRoute. Reads then use<br/>createServerSupabase (service role).

    alt No valid session
        Actions-->>Profile: 401 'Sign in to view profiles.'
        Profile-->>Steward: Show error
    else Access allowed
        Actions->>DB: Read people (display_name, skills, focus_areas) with socials<br/>(email, phone, website, instagram, facebook, x, linkedin)<br/>by id = personId, or by auth_user_id = session user
        activate DB
        DB-->>Actions: people row or no row
        deactivate DB
        alt No profile for this user
            Actions-->>Profile: Not found (404)
            Profile-->>Steward: Show "Profile not found"
        else Profile found
            Note right of Actions: Role read from auth app_metadata.role, display only.<br/>If people.auth_user_id is null, the route returns<br/>zero stats and runs no inspection queries.
            par SIR history and count (1.0.3 AT1, 1.0.4)
                Actions->>DB: form_responses (is_active, user_id = people.auth_user_id)<br/>with sites_pa name, count exact, range 10 per page
            and Distinct sites (1.0.4)
                Actions->>DB: rpc get_distinct_inspected_site_count(p_user_id)
            end
            activate DB
            DB-->>Actions: SIR page, inspectionCount, distinctSiteCount
            deactivate DB
            Actions-->>Profile: profile, isOwner, stats {inspectionCount, distinctSiteCount},<br/>history, pagination
            Profile-->>Steward: Show profile, quick stats and SIR history
        end
    end
    deactivate Actions

    Profile->>StewardActions: getSitesForSteward(people.id)
    activate StewardActions
    StewardActions->>DB: site_stewards join sites_pa(namesite) where steward_id
    activate DB
    DB-->>StewardActions: Stewarded sites
    deactivate DB
    StewardActions-->>Profile: Site list
    deactivate StewardActions
    Profile-->>Steward: Show "Steward of" site links
    Note over Profile,DB: Data is read again on each load, with no cache (1.0.1 AT5).<br/>A new SIR adds 1 to the count on next load (1.0.4 AT2).

    opt Open a past SIR (1.0.3 AT2, AT3)
        Steward->>Profile: Select a SIR in the history
        Profile->>Pages: Open /detail/[namesite] of that SIR's site (not scrolled to the SIR)
        Pages->>StewardActions: getFormResponsesBySite(namesite) in utils/supabase/queries.ts<br/>(exists, no session check today)
        activate StewardActions
        StewardActions->>StewardActions: Same session check (Proposed)
        StewardActions->>DB: Read form_responses and answers
        activate DB
        DB-->>StewardActions: SIR answers
        deactivate DB
        StewardActions->>StewardActions: Remove answers listed in<br/>profile_hidden_questions (Proposed)
        StewardActions-->>Pages: Visible answers only
        deactivate StewardActions
        Pages-->>Steward: Show the SIR
    end

    opt Go back (1.0.1 AT4)
        Steward->>Profile: Select Back
        Profile-->>Steward: Go to previous page: router.back(),<br/>or /sites if there is no history
    end
    deactivate Profile

    Note over Steward,DB: Only active web SIRs (form_responses.is_active) are counted.<br/>Open questions: which answers count as "activities",<br/>and how a steward marks answers as hidden.
